I don't "decide" to become a walking tank.  It just kinda happens as a
result of various independent decisions.

I collect a nice weapon because it lets me kill things faster.

I collect MR because without it my nice shiny armour will get blasted to
dust and Rodney (and arch-liches and Death) can turn me into a corpse on
the spot.

I collect reflection because then disint res doesn't matter unless I get
stupid, and my possessions are protected from fire, cold, and lightning.

I collect good armour and alchemise healing potions into full healing
because it makes me harder to hurt and need more hurting in order to
kill.

I collect teleport control and teleportation magic to make travel
quicker.

The reason Gehennom is boring is that the nature of the environment acts
to limit the threat presented by most monsters.  A horde isn't terribly
dangerous if only two of them can get at you at once.  Fire, Water, Air,
and Astral are quite exciting, of course, especially for wombats.

I want Gehennom to make me have to *think*; right now Gehennom as a
whole demands less thought than most levels of the Dungeons of Doom
demand individually.

